# Agent workflow

Follow `docs/AGENT_WORKFLOW.md`.

## Parallelism (good)

Read-only: trace paths, search regressions, inspect tests, compare commits, review schema/UI/security/diff. These may be separate explore subagents.

## Parallelism (bad)

Multiple agents **editing** the same payment engine, tickets, checkout, or fulfilment. For critical payment logic: **one implementation owner** integrates the fix. Others may investigate/review only.

## Worktrees

Use isolated worktrees only for truly independent work (docs vs unrelated module). Do **not** split tightly coupled payment changes across worktrees.

## Pre-task (payment-sensitive)

Read applicable `.cursor/rules`, identify critical flows, inspect current code, confirm/run `npm run test:payments:fast` if appropriate, state exact scope, then edit.

## Post-task (payment-sensitive)

Targeted tests → fast suite → full suite before completion → git diff → verify Live flag untouched → typecheck/build → TEST deploy if appropriate → live browser QA → report unverified items explicitly.
